WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:04.188
What is the "Conjunction of the Spheres" in
the world of "The Witcher"?

00:00:04.188 --> 00:00:07.010
Simply put, it's what it's like when worlds
collide.

00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:11.750
Geralt of Rivia goes up against a number of
bloodthirsty monsters throughout the dangerous

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:17.619
world of Netflix's "The Witcher," and these
encounters give many episodes a horrific flair.

00:00:17.619 --> 00:00:21.580
As if that wasn't enough, there's the fact
that whenever Ciri screams, she unleashes

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:26.530
other terrifying monsters from inside the
black monoliths scattered around the Continent.

00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:30.269
That's all without mentioning the political
intrigue, the Northern Kingdoms' war with

00:00:30.269 --> 00:00:34.989
Nilfgaard, and Geralt's complicated romance
with Yennefer of Vengerberg.

00:00:34.989 --> 00:00:40.210
Season 2 deepens the lore behind the Continent,
as Yennefer, Fringilla, and Francesca are

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:44.899
all wrapped up in a dark conspiracy to resurrect
a malevolent demon called Voleth Meir.

00:00:44.899 --> 00:00:51.825
The show also briefly touches on why the Continent
is crammed with humans, elves, dwarves, and monsters.

00:00:51.825 --> 00:00:56.510
For this history, it calls back to an event
long ago in the timeline called the Conjunction

00:00:56.510 --> 00:00:58.010
of the Spheres.

00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:02.160
In "The Witcher" books by Andrzej Sapkowski,
the Conjunction of the Spheres takes place

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:07.380
more than a thousand years before Geralt's
adventures with Vesemir, Yennefer, and Ciri.

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:11.870
In fact, it's the reason why the Continent
is such a dangerous place to live, as the

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:14.000
"The Witcher 3: Wild Hunt" explains.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:19.210
"In a time past, our world intertwined with
another through an upheaval scholars call

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:22.096
the Conjunction of the Spheres."

00:01:22.096 --> 00:01:25.860
The cataclysmic event caused different universes
to crash into one another.

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:30.640
And it brought a countless number of other
beings into the world, like all the monsters

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:32.860
that Geralt and his friends go up against
in "The Witcher."

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:37.860
It also brought separate races of human beings
into the Continent, with different languages

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:38.860
and customs.

00:01:39.059 --> 00:01:43.749
"Its survivors, lost and forsaken in a new
world."

00:01:44.182 --> 00:01:45.550
"New to you."

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:50.000
Monsters and humans weren't the only things
to come through the Conjunction of the Spheres, though.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.649
The disaster also brought magic and chaos
into the Continent.

00:01:53.649 --> 00:01:58.070
Eventually, humans realized they could tap
into the mysterious force to cast spells,

00:01:58.070 --> 00:02:01.170
which is how the Brotherhood of Sorcerers
got started.

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:05.570
Humans also decided to stake their claim on
this new world for themselves, and surprised

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:06.843
the elves with their savagery.

00:02:06.843 --> 00:02:09.189
As a bit of lore text from the games recounts,

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:24.030
A second Conjunction briefly happens in "The
Witcher 3: The Wild Hunt."

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:28.490
It once again brings new creatures into the
world, and even causes the elves to leave

00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:31.580
the Continent in search of a new realm to
call home.

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:35.090
Because the Conjunction of the Spheres is
such a pivotal event in the history of the

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:40.933
Continent, Netflix is diving into that era
with a spin-off series called "The Witcher: Blood Origin."

00:02:40.933 --> 00:02:45.290
It's set right before the Conjunction of the
Spheres and will look at how the elven empire

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:47.739
collapses after the disaster takes place.

00:02:47.739 --> 00:02:52.200
"Blood Origin" will also reveal how the Conjunction
happened in the first place, and it'll even

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.170
explain how the first Witcher was created.

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:58.180
So, it's going to be a must-watch for fans
who want to learn more about the Continent.

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:03.060
"Iron Fist" writer Declan de Barra is the
showrunner on "Blood Origin," and "The Witcher"

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:07.549
showrunner Lauren S. Hissrich is also an executive
producer on the series.

00:03:07.549 --> 00:03:11.690
This means it'll all fit nicely together in
the timeline, and it should hopefully answer

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:14.709
some key questions that fans have about the
universe.

00:03:14.709 --> 00:03:16.360
Hissrich told Entertainment Weekly,

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:33.370
Netflix has amassed an impressive cast for
"Blood Origin," including "Crouching Tiger,

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:38.142
Hidden Dragon" and "Everything Everywhere
All at Once" star Michelle Yeoh in a lead role.

00:03:38.189 --> 00:03:43.797
Luckily there isn't long to wait, since "Blood
Origin" arrives on Christmas Day, 2022.

